    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "Find the least integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > such that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed914d211481f6024950445b535570b33446a9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2011 \\times 2011$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"13\" > table filled with integers Kain chooses, Abel be able to change at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > cells to achieve a new table in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8d983596f717d941d13f85fa40f4832b3624c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4022$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" > sums of rows and columns are pairwise different.",
    "post_canonical": "Find the least integer $k$ such that for any $2011 \\times 2011$ table filled with integers Kain chooses, Abel be able to change at most $k$ cells to achieve a new table in which $4022$ sums of rows and columns are pairwise different. ",
