    "topic_id": 2061174,
    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" > be positive real numbers with <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25c63ce930f2589378f70d60e3984873e6cc344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2 \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" >.</span> Prove that:<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/362532c5d1916835c29158a679cd18b72228c2ef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$\\frac{(a+1)(b+2)}{(b+1)(b+5)}+\\frac{(b+1)(c+2)}{(c+1)(c+5)}+\\frac{(c+1)(a+2)}{(a+1)(a+5)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}.$$\"  width=\"420\" height=\"43\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Let $a,b,c$ be positive real numbers with $a^2+b^2+c^2 \\geq 3$. Prove that: \n$$\\frac{(a+1)(b+2)}{(b+1)(b+5)}+\\frac{(b+1)(c+2)}{(c+1)(c+5)}+\\frac{(c+1)(a+2)}{(a+1)(a+5)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}.$$",
